How can I efficiently find the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2 using MATLAB? Also, can you provide a solution that can handle a large amount of text? 
Here's an implementation in MATLAB that can handle large text:
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt'); %read text1 from file
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt'); %read text2 from file
%Convert text to lowercase and split into words
words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));
%Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);
%Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);

response:
Your MATLAB code is a good starting point for finding unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2. Here's an optimized version that can handle large amounts of text more efficiently:

```matlab
function uniqueWords = findUniqueWords(text1, text2)
    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
    words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));

    % Create a set data type to store unique words
    uniqueWords = cell(1, 0);

    % Use a hash table (a.k.a. dictionary or map) to efficiently check if a word is unique
    wordMap = table();

    % Iterate over words1 and add them to the hash table
    for i = 1:numel(words1)
        word = words1{i};

        % Check if the word is already in the hash table
        if ~ismember(word, wordMap)
            % Add the word to the hash table and the unique words list
            wordMap{word} = true;
            uniqueWords{end+1} = word;
        end
    end

    % Iterate over words2 and remove any unique words that are also in text2
    for i = 1:numel(words2)
        word = words2{i};

        % Check if the word is in the hash table and remove it if it is
        if ismember(word, wordMap)
            % Remove the word from the unique words list
            uniqueWords = uniqueWords(uniqueWords ~= word);
        end
    end
end
```

This function uses a hash table to efficiently check if a word is unique, which is much faster than iterating over the entire array of words. It also removes any unique words that are also in text2, which further improves the efficiency.

